On Thursday, February 1, 2024 at 9:00:18 PM UTC-8 luis.m...@gmail.com wrote:
> Hi Gabriella,
>
> - For a tutorial of RDA see: https://popgen.nescent.org/2018-03-27_RDA_GEA.html
> - Australia's Bureau of meteorology (BOM) has tons of environmental data that is freely available: Australia's official weather forecasts & weather radar - Bureau of Meteorology (bom.gov.au) <http://www.bom.gov.au/>
> - For other methods check this paper: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.gene.2021.146165
> - You could also try outflank (see function gl.outflank) or bayescan (see function gl2bayescan).
> - If you have a reference genome and a GFF file, you could filter out coding regions (after blasting your SNPs)
